e six figures  out of college and over 200 000 by the  time they're 30. now you might be saying  that these Junior Consultants are  usually led by senior Consultants who do  know what they're doing but to that I  would argue that most companies have  internal staff that are more  knowledgeable than senior consultants  for example an internal program manager  who has 20 years of experience across  four or five big companies in a specific  domain will likely outperform a Senior  Management Consultant with a broad  experience every day of the week hearing  all this you're probably wondering why  in the world do top consulting firms  pull in tens of billions if they're so  useless well one thing's for sure and  not for their management expertise so  here's why companies actually hire  management Consultants  foreign  reasons that companies hire Consultants  aren't to break through various barriers  both internally and externally if you're  a high-ranking executive at a 10 plus  billion dollar company you're probably  going to have to handle a bunch of  politics this includes things like a  backstabbing and a blackmailing  colleagues trash talking competent  employees and intentionally withholding  crucial information why do people resort  to such measures you ask well it usually  has to do with the jealousy ego and  getting revenge for example Betty Who  works across from you and is obviously  less productive may get that promotion  before you do and suddenly you have to  report to Betty from your perspective it  Betty doesn't deserve that title and  you're honestly pretty salty that you  didn't get the promotion yourself so the  next time that Betty tells you to do  something you may be inclined to be  unresponsive push back or put up  unnecessary roadblocks usually you can't  justify such employees because you'd end  up laying off your entire Workforce not  to mention it in most cases such  employees aren't necessarily incompetent  or not hard working they just need  